0dfc32dc26937551c6d7c9d448ac76ea93362351e24a34762f4e11af417d0d77  rule-resolved-1

# The pinned hash of the context pack every round supplies alongside the question.
#
# It is the SHA-256 of the ordered list of (path, sha256) anchors that the rule in
# tools/round_cycle.py CONTEXT_PACK resolves to -- not of the rendered prose, so the
# pin survives a change in how the pack is formatted and breaks when the DOCUMENTS
# change, which is what matters.
#
# WHY A PIN AND NOT A CLAIM. The prompt used to tell every party that the pack was
# "FIXED and identical for every round". That was false. The RULE is fixed; the bytes
# it resolves to drift as the repository changes, so two rounds could see different
# evidence with nothing recording that they had. Pinning converts the drift from a
# silent event into an explicit decision: the cycle refuses until someone re-pins.
#
# TO RE-PIN, deliberately: run `python3 tools/round_cycle.py --selector rotation
# --dry-run`, take the current hash from the refusal, and replace the line above in
# the same commit as whatever changed the pack. A re-pin that arrives in its own
# commit with no explanation is the control being routed around.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT ACHIEVE. The pack was never pre-committed at the time the
# proposals were solicited, so for the twenty-four questions already in the queue it
# is pinned-before-selection, not pinned-at-submission. The stronger scheme -- each
# proposal carrying its own hash-addressed evidence manifest, refused rather than
# trimmed when it exceeds the ceiling -- applies from the next agenda solicitation
# onward and is recorded in the SOP.
